-- Repeated map/filter/fold passes over moderate lists.
--
-- STRESSES (deliberately, an aspect that WILL change): per-activation graph
-- allocation. Each pass builds a fresh range, a mapped list, a filtered list,
-- and folds it — every element is a freshly allocated RuntimeCons / NamedThunk.
-- The builder VM (mode=compiled) removes the AST re-traversal but, by design,
-- still materializes the same graph (BYTECODE.md §3). So this is the workload
-- whose interp-vs-compiled gap should stay SMALL today and only widen once the
-- deferred direct-reduction machine (§15.1) eliminates graph allocation. Track
-- it as a regression sentinel for that future work.
--
-- Chunked into 175 passes of 4000 so no single fold forces a pathologically
-- deep thunk; the work, not the depth, is what scales.
import core, list, math in
let
  pass = seed -> range 1 4000 > map (mul 3) > filter even > sum
in
range 1 175 > map pass > sum > show
